        {
            "block_label": "table",
            "block_content": "<table><tr><td>Element Name</td><td>Type</td><td>Semantics</td></tr><tr><td>Header</td><td>complexType: MessageHeaderType Refer to 8.3.3</td><td>Contains general information, used for all messages.</td></tr><tr><td>ResponseCode</td><td>simpleType: responseCodeType enumeration refer to Annex A for the type definition</td><td>ResponseCode indicating the acknowledgment status of any of the V2G messages received by the SECC.</td></tr><tr><td>EVSEProcessing</td><td>simpleType: processingType enumeration refer to Annex A for the type definition</td><td>Parameter indicating that the EVSE has finished the processing that was initiated after the ScheduleExchangeReq. Alternatively, this parameter can indicate that the EVSE is still processing at the time that the response message was sent.</td></tr><tr><td>GoToPause</td><td>simpleType: xs:boolean</td><td>Optional: When GoToPause is set to TRUE, this indicates that the EVSE does not have any power available and the EVCC can therefore directly go to PowerDeliveryReq.</td></tr><tr><td>Dynamic_SEResControlMode</td><td>complexType: Dynamic_SEResControlModeType refer to 8.3.5.3.15</td><td>Includes price schedule for the session. Includes departure time in case EVSE provides it.</td></tr><tr><td>Scheduled_SEResControlMode</td><td>complexType: Scheduled_SEResControlModeType refer to 8.3.5.3.16</td><td>Includes several tuples of schedules from secondary actors. The SECC shall only omit the parameter &quot;ScheduleList&quot; in case EVSEProcessing is set to &quot;Ongoing&quot;.</td></tr></table>",
            "block_bbox": [
                79,
